# Valgrind suppressions for the valgrind job in .github/workflows/native-checks.yaml.
#
# tools/ is in .Rbuildignore, so nothing here reaches the tarball or CRAN.
#
# One entry, and the block is cli's, not this package's. testthat reports
# progress through cli, and cli starts a timer thread (pthread_create in
# cli.so) that lives until the process exits. glibc allocates that thread's
# thread-local storage (_dl_allocate_tls, 368 bytes here) when the thread is
# made; a thread still running at exit leaves it allocated, and valgrind
# reports it as "possibly lost" because the only pointer to it is in the
# thread's own descriptor. Nothing is lost and nothing in zudedup is
# involved.
#
# It first appeared at Stage 4 (2026-10-08), when the heavy tests made the
# suite run long enough under valgrind (32 minutes) for the thread to be
# started. Definitely and indirectly lost were 0, with no invalid access.
#
# Scoped to a possible leak whose allocation comes from pthread_create called
# from cli.so, so a real leak anywhere else is still reported.
{
   cli-timer-thread-tls
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: possible
   fun:calloc
   ...
   fun:_dl_allocate_tls
   ...
   fun:pthread_create*
   obj:*/cli/libs/cli.so
}
